Answer NO_ASSIGNMENT and UNREGISTERED_USER Server-Assignment-Requests as TS
29.228 6.1.2.1 has them.

The SAR callback downloaded User-Data only for REGISTRATION and RE_REGISTRATION.
NO_ASSIGNMENT and UNREGISTERED_USER are sent precisely to get the profile -- the
first by an S-CSCF restoring a user it lost (TS 23.380 4.4.2), the second for a
terminating request to an unregistered user -- and both got a DIAMETER_SUCCESS
with no User-Data, which the S-CSCF (kamailio's ims_registrar_scscf) fails as
"We require User data for this assignment/register and none was supplied".

NO_ASSIGNMENT also assigns nothing: it is answered only for the S-CSCF already
assigned to the user, and any other gets DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY with the
stored Server-Name left alone. The callback instead overwrote the Server-Name
for every type before looking at which one it was, so a NO_ASSIGNMENT from a
second S-CSCF would have moved the user to it. The type is now read first: a
NO_ASSIGNMENT from anyone but the assigned S-CSCF is refused, and only the
other types overwrite. DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY is a base protocol code, so it
goes out as a Result-Code rather than through the Experimental-Result the
error path otherwise uses.

diff --git a/src/hss/hss-cx-path.c b/src/hss/hss-cx-path.c
index a9c72d6..689091d 100644
--- a/src/hss/hss-cx-path.c
+++ b/src/hss/hss-cx-path.c
@@ -1080,6 +1080,7 @@ static int hss_ogs_diam_cx_sar_cb(struct msg **msg, struct avp *avp,
 
     ogs_ims_data_t ims_data;
     int error_occurred = 0;
+    int unable_to_comply = 0;
 
     ogs_debug("Rx Server-Assignment-Request");
 
@@ -1268,8 +1269,29 @@ static int hss_ogs_diam_cx_sar_cb(struct msg **msg, struct avp *avp,
         goto out;
     }
 
-    /* Overwrite Server-Name for IMPU(Public-Identity) */
-    hss_cx_set_server_name(public_identity, server_name, true);
+    /*
+     * NO_ASSIGNMENT asks for the profile and nothing else: it assigns no
+     * S-CSCF, and it is answered only for the S-CSCF already assigned. Any
+     * other gets DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY and the stored name is left alone
+     * (TS 29.228 6.1.2.1, TS 23.380 4.4.2) -- which is what tells an S-CSCF
+     * that lost its data to have the UE register again.
+     */
+    ret = fd_msg_search_avp(qry, ogs_diam_cx_server_assignment_type, &avp);
+    if (ret == 0 && avp && fd_msg_avp_hdr(avp, &hdr) == 0 && hdr &&
+            hdr->avp_value->i32 == OGS_DIAM_CX_SERVER_NO_ASSIGNMENT) {
+        char *assigned = hss_cx_get_server_name(public_identity);
+        if (!assigned || strcmp(assigned, server_name) != 0) {
+            ogs_warn("NO_ASSIGNMENT from [%s] for [%s] assigned to [%s]",
+                    server_name, public_identity,
+                    assigned ? assigned : "none");
+            unable_to_comply = 1;
+            error_occurred = 1;
+            goto out;
+        }
+    } else {
+        /* Overwrite Server-Name for IMPU(Public-Identity) */
+        hss_cx_set_server_name(public_identity, server_name, true);
+    }
 
     if (!error_occurred) {
         /* Set Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP */
@@ -1359,9 +1381,17 @@ static int hss_ogs_diam_cx_sar_cb(struct msg **msg, struct avp *avp,
             goto out;
         }
 
+        /*
+         * The profile goes with every assignment that sets up service for the
+         * user, not only registration: NO_ASSIGNMENT and UNREGISTERED_USER are
+         * both asked for precisely to download it (TS 29.228 6.1.2.1).
+         */
         if (hdr->avp_value->i32 == OGS_DIAM_CX_SERVER_ASSIGNMENT_REGISTRATION ||
             hdr->avp_value->i32 ==
-                OGS_DIAM_CX_SERVER_ASSIGNMENT_RE_REGISTRATION) {
+                OGS_DIAM_CX_SERVER_ASSIGNMENT_RE_REGISTRATION ||
+            hdr->avp_value->i32 == OGS_DIAM_CX_SERVER_NO_ASSIGNMENT ||
+            hdr->avp_value->i32 ==
+                OGS_DIAM_CX_SERVER_ASSIGNMENT_UNREGISTERED_USER) {
 
             /* Get User-Data-Already-Available AVP (Mandatory) */
             ret = fd_msg_search_avp(
@@ -1503,7 +1533,11 @@ out:
                 ans, OGS_DIAM_CX_APPLICATION_ID);
 
         /* Set the Experimental-Result, Origin-Host and Origin-Realm AVPs */
-        if (result_code != 0) {
+        if (unable_to_comply) {
+            /* a base protocol code, so a Result-Code, not Experimental */
+            ret = fd_msg_rescode_set(ans,
+                    (char*)"DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY", NULL, NULL, 1);
+        } else if (result_code != 0) {
             ret = ogs_diam_message_experimental_rescode_set(ans, result_code);
         }
 
